1
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:39,333
La Ronde is a drama film directed by Sophie Goyette.

2
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:12,666
Twin siblings deal with their father’s imminent death: Alexandre feels the
need to stay while Ariane has an uncontrollable urge to leave.

3
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
La Ronde is a Canadian short drama film, directed by
Sophie Goyette and released in 2011.

4
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:19,333
The film stars Éliane Préfontaine and Hubert Lemire as Ariane and Alexandre, twin siblings who are experiencing very different reactions to
their father's impending death: Alexandre feels the need to stay close to their father, while Ariane feels the need to leave.

5
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:52,666
The film premiered at the Locarno Film Festival on August 6, 2011, and had its
Canadian premiere at the 2011 Toronto International Film Festival.

6
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
The film was named to TIFF's year-end Canada's Top Ten list for 2011, and was a Genie
Award nominee for Best Live Action Short Drama at the 32nd Genie Awards.

7
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:59,333
Goyette's feature film debut, Still Night, Still Light (Mes nuits feront écho), starred
Préfontaine in a thematically similar story about a different character.

8
00:20:26,666 --> 00:20:32,666
The tone is emotional.
